      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a8b57d97f57fad85f3c0d123d817ad5c1ff9876662c9d11fbac203530e20f851",
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Salta. On arrival, set off for Cafayate, a drive of about three hours.\n\nCafayate is one of north-west Argentina's best-known wine towns. After the long drive, the contrast between the dry mountain scenery and the green vineyards is striking. At one of the main wine estates, your guide will explain how the vines are tended, how the grapes are harvested, and how different types of wine are made and aged. You'll then have free time to walk around town among the wineries and vineyards and take in the surrounding valley at your own pace.\n\nLunch in the main square is paid for separately. You'll also visit the wine museum and spend the night at a wine hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-mw9gatwi",
        "model": "ChatGPT Codex"
      }
    },
